  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Spirit Affinity House presents Zhao Lian Yun at a Thieving Heaven Demon Venerable inheritance entrance. Zhao Lian Yun accepts the rank nine immortal killer move divine concealment, and also obtains a clue that another Thieving Heaven inheritance about ghostly concealment is hidden in Luo Po Valley. Rumors name divine concealment and ghostly concealment as Thieving Heaven Demon Venerable’s two defensive killer moves.",
      "chapters": [
        949
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_spirit_affinity_house",
        "char_zhao_lian_yun",
        "char_thieving_heaven_demon_venerable",
        "loc_luo_po_valley"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan enters a Thieving Heaven true inheritance space in Luo Po Valley and obtains ghostly concealment.",
      "chapters": [
        991
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "luo-po-inheritance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Lang Ya land spirit states that Thieving Heaven left many inheritances but only ten true inheritances, each an unparalleled treasure holding the essence of his cultivation, and that the inheritor must be an otherworldly demon. Legend names divine concealment and ghostly concealment as a paired defensive set: divine concealment hides from deductions of thoughts, wills, and emotions, while ghostly concealment is tied to the soul; obtaining one yields clues to the other.",
      "chapters": [
        992
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "true-inheritance-rules",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_lang_ya_land_spirit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Lang Ya land spirit offers three true inheritances in trade and ranks the Thieving Heaven true inheritance as the least valuable of the three, while noting that Thieving Heaven’s true inheritances come in pairs and that he left ten in total. Only otherworldly demons can receive most of them; the copy in Lang Ya’s hands is the exception.",
      "chapters": [
        1051
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "lang-ya-copy",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_lang_ya_sect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Of Thieving Heaven’s true inheritances, Fang Yuan has only inherited ghostly concealment, while divine concealment was taken by Zhao Lian Yun.",
      "chapters": [
        1435
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "holder-confirmation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lang Ya blessed land holds Thieving Heaven’s true inheritance among three great true inheritances, and rank eight steal life Immortal Gu is part of it; in Fang Yuan’s previous life, Ma Hong Yun used clues from that inheritance to have Lang Ya refine Gu three times.",
      "chapters": [
        1758
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "core-immortal-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_lang_ya_blessed_land",
        "gu_steal_life_gu",
        "char_ma_hong_yun"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan researches that Lang Ya Thieving Heaven true inheritance: its core is steal life Immortal Gu and the method to unseal it, plus theft path fundamentals, and he finds it short beside Giant Sun’s self luck true inheritance.",
      "chapters": [
        1782
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "lang-ya-research-core",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "inh_self_luck_true_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang clan also holds a Thieving Heaven true inheritance whose essence is the killer move steal dao and which records the theft path Immortal Gu House Thieves Den; Fang Yuan browses that content after Fang clan agrees.",
      "chapters": [
        1857
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fang-clan-copy",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_fang_clan",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "house_thieves_den"
      ]
    }
  ],
